      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A true advocate for the working family would argue that the government's primary, non-negotiable duty is to its own constituents. They would assert that while global issues are tragic, the immediate suffering of citizens struggling with crumbling roads or underfunded schools must take absolute precedence. From this viewpoint, every dollar sent overseas is a dollar stolen directly from the needs of American families. This perspective frames foreign aid as a luxury we cannot afford when our own house is burning down.",
      "source": "target",
